&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations across the GTM stack using middleware (Workato) and native connectors: CPQ, conversation intelligence, chat, dialer, enrichment, and partner platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-administer DealHub CPQ with our Deal Desk, keeping quote-to-order flowing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond quickly to revenue-blocking issues, especially at month and quarter end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own data quality across the revenue stack: deduplication, enrichment, routing integrity, and regular audits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document what you build and enable sales users, partnering with RevOps and Enablement on rollout and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-7+ years administering CRM and GTM systems at a B2B SaaS company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience administering HubSpot: data model and objects, pipelines, workflows and automation, permissions, and reporting; experience with other CRM ecosystems is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration experience: middleware such as Workato (strongly preferred) or similar, native connectors, and comfort working with APIs and webhooks when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quote-to-cash familiarity: CPQ administration (DealHub or similar) and how quoting, ordering, and billing hang together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a migration or dual-run environment: disciplined about change management, sandboxes, and testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security-minded: SSO app configuration and least-privilege permissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator who partners well with Sales, Deal Desk, and RevOps stakeholders under time pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HubSpot certifications (e.g., HubSpot Revenue Operations Certification, HubSpot Administration Certification), Workato Automation Pro, and familiarity with tools like Gong, Qualified, or PartnerStack are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
