&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Pantheon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pantheon brings together exceptional builders who take ownership, drive meaningful impact, and shape what&#39;s next for the web. We power more than 300,000 websites globally for organizations including Google, Princeton, Salesloft, Clorox, and the United Nations. Every day, thousands of developers and marketers use our WebOps platform to build, iterate, and scale WordPress, Drupal, and Next.js sites that reach billions of people worldwide. As an employer, we operate with the same philosophy that drives our product: foundation and freedom. Pantheon is a vibrant, remote-forward team of experts who care deeply about their craft and results. Here, you take ownership of work that matters, contribute alongside exceptional people, and see the impact you create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own Developer Experience—a strategic product area that includes some of Pantheon&#39;s biggest differentiators: Autopilot, Multidev, and Upstreams. You&#39;ll define strategy across this disparate set of products while stewarding expansion into high-impact areas: public API, MCP integrations, and agentic infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role that executes a plan; it co-authors one. You&#39;ll serve developers and their teams—from individual contributors to engineering leaders—ensuring they can build, test, collaborate, and deploy with speed and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need to Succeed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize a diverse product portfolio into a cohesive strategy that multiplies developer productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the roadmap for emerging areas—public APIs, MCPs, agentic systems—where you&#39;ll shape what&#39;s possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand developer workflows deeply: local development, collaboration, testing, CI/CD integration, and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather research and competitive intelligence to identify high-leverage opportunities across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics that connect developer velocity and satisfaction to business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate strategy and progress with clarity to engineering, product, and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of industry experience, including 3+ years managing developer-facing products or platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage a broad, complex product portfolio and unify disparate pieces into strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of developer workflows: Git, CI/CD, testing, collaboration, deployment, and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping integrations or platform APIs; familiarity with emerging technologies (AI agents, MCPs, agentic systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record taking products from strategy through launch and iterative improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence cross-functional teams and navigate organizational complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: Experience at a developer platform (GitHub, GitLab, Vercel, Netlify, LaunchDarkly, etc.); hands-on knowledge of WordPress, Drupal, or modern frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
