&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pantheon is building the next generation of web content infrastructure — a real-time, collaborative platform that redefines how teams create, publish, and manage content on the modern web. Content management has been largely unchanged for two decades. Pantheon is uniquely positioned — with deep roots in the web platform, a global CDN, and a sophisticated branching model trusted by thousands of organizations — to build the collaborative content experience the modern web deserves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to join a founding-stage product team at a company with real infrastructure and real distribution behind it. The architecture is being defined now. The decisions made in the next few months will shape how developers and content teams experience the web for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer on this team, you will be a technical anchor and a hands-on builder. You will own significant pieces of the platform end-to-end — from API design and backend services to frontend systems and browser-side experiences. You will partner closely with the Staff Engineer and Director of Engineering to make architectural decisions, set quality standards, and accelerate the team toward meaningful milestones.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both breadth and depth. You are comfortable owning a problem from design through delivery, writing the code and the tests, and helping less experienced engineers do the same. You understand that great infrastructure and great product experience are not in tension — they are the same problem viewed from different angles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Need to Succeed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own significant features and platform components end-to-end — from technical design through production delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build backend services, APIs, and frontend systems that power a real-time collaborative content platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute meaningfully to architectural decisions — your opinion matters and will be sought&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested code and help establish quality standards for the team — there is no dedicated QA on this team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support SE II engineers through code review, pairing, and technical guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and design to translate ambiguous requirements into concrete technical plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate AI tooling concretely into your development workflow and into the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define how the team works — process, standards, and engineering culture are all being built right now&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Bring to the Table&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8 years of professional software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine full-stack capability — you have shipped production systems on both backend (APIs, cloud infrastructure, data services) and frontend (component systems, browser performance, interactive UIs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong API design experience: REST, GraphQL, and webhooks — with opinions about when to use each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud-native fluency: you have designed and operated services in GCP, AWS, or Azure, not just deployed to them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or collaborative systems is a meaningful plus — live data sync, multiplayer state, event-driven architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend architecture depth: component modeling, state management, rendering performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are actively and concretely building with AI — integrating it into products you own or creating tooling that makes AI more effective.&lt;/li&gt;
